## Supplement 2026-05-03 — compatibility ledger + Postgres offset retention

- Compatibility ledger: Phase 10 API rows use `"failure_modes": "untested"` (contract test `ledger_has_required_profiles_and_storage_tiers`).
- LibSQL `LiteStorage::maintain`: expiry delete runs `execute("consumer_offset_delete_expired.sql", …)` so the statement cache resolves embedded SQL.
- Postgres DDL: `consumer_offset.expires_at` in `etc/initdb.d/010-schema.sql`; idempotent `etc/initdb.d/011-offset-retention-patch.sql`; `jansu-storage` tests call `ensure_postgres_offset_schema` before `build_storage`.
- `PgStorage::create_topic`: insert initial leader epoch via `tx_prepare_execute` with `&0_i32` / `&0_i64` (avoids `query_raw` on non-`RETURNING` insert and bigint bind mismatch).
- `offset_retention_cleanup_round_trip`: now `(storage, cluster_id, node_id)` so `register_broker` matches `Storage::cluster` used by `create_topic`.
- Verified: `just compatibility-contract`, `just check`, `cargo nextest run -p jansu-storage --test consumer_offsets --all-features` (6/6 including Postgres). Full `jansu-broker` `pg::` nextest slice not re-run in this session (host disk ENOSPC during link).

